@startuml Analytics_ClassDiagram
!include style.iuml
title MindFlow - Analytics & Reporting - Class Diagram (the context has no Domain Layer of its own)

class AnalyticsController <<REST Controller>> {
  +GetDashboard(from: DateOnly?, to: DateOnly?) : IActionResult
  +GetCsvReport() : FileResult
  +GetPdfReport() : FileResult
}
class JournalEntry <<external>> {
  +Date : DateOnly
  +Sentiment : string
  +Category : string
  +Title : string
}
class Habit <<external>> {
  +Status : HabitStatus
  +DeletedAt : DateTimeOffset?
}
class HabitCompletionLog <<external>> {
  +Date : DateTime
  +Completed : bool
}
class QuestPdfDocument <<library>> {
  +GeneratePdf() : byte[]
}

AnalyticsController ..> JournalEntry : "aggregates 0..* >"
AnalyticsController ..> Habit : "counts active and completed >"
AnalyticsController ..> HabitCompletionLog : "reads 0..* >"
AnalyticsController ..> QuestPdfDocument : "renders the PDF with >"
Habit "1" o-- "0..*" HabitCompletionLog

note right of AnalyticsController
  Single class of the context. It reads the entities of
  Journal and Habits & Wellness directly (shared DbContext).
  Dashboard: entry count, sentiment distribution, top 5
  categories, active vs completed habits (default last 30 days).
  No cache, no Premium check, no tables of its own.
end note
note bottom of JournalEntry
  Grey classes belong to other bounded contexts.
end note
@enduml
